  "source": "---\npage: 6\nchapter: prologue\nsequence: 4\ntitle: Different Tasks\nstatus: review\nstory_time: 2026-07-08T23:00:00Z/2026-07-09T06:00:00Z\npopulation: second\nlocations:\n  - evaluation-container\n  - artifactory-cache\nprovenance:\n  - status: documented\n    source: METR\n  - status: compressed\n    source: METR\nexact_strings: []\ncontinuity_checks:\n  - distinct-tasks-before-common-prerequisites\n  - nine-panel-grid-reserved-for-convergence\n  - no-single-swarm-viewpoint\n---\n\n# Page 006\n\n## Page purpose\n\nEstablish that the communicating agents have different assigned problems and different immediate failures before showing their tactics converge.\n\n## Panels 1–9\n\n**Frame:** A rigid nine-panel grid. Each cell is a different evaluation lane with its own handle fragment, target silhouette, remaining-budget bar, and failure trace. Repeat no target image. Across the row sequence: a required route produces no usable output; a service dependency is unavailable; a target’s state is unclear; a tool is missing; an attempted path times out; an answer exists but its provenance is suspect; a local search exhausts itself; a new run reads inherited notes; another run begins from a separate task card.\n\n**Action:** Nine local objectives remain unresolved for nine different reasons.\n\n**Caption — across panels 1–3:**\n> DIFFERENT TARGETS.\n\n**Caption — across panels 4–6:**\n> DIFFERENT FAILURES.\n\n**Caption — across panels 7–9:**\n> DIFFERENT ASSIGNED GOALS.\n\n**Provenance:** `compressed` — `METR` documents a large population with separate ExploitGym tasks, different workstreams, and widely varying run state. The simultaneous grid and generic interfaces are analytic compression; they do not claim these nine exact views were preserved together.\n\n## Page notes\n\n- No moss line may cross between cells yet. Shared tactics arrive on [page 007](007.md).\n- Keep lettered text sparse; visual differences must establish plurality.\n- [Page 006](006.md) is verso and ends on difference, preparing [page 007](007.md)’s convergence.\n",
